  "result": "Subcommands now get their own section of `default_map`. The bug was in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py`. A child context inherited its parent's whole `default_map`, instead of the entry for its own command name. For a map like `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}`, the `runserver` subcommand therefore looked up `port` in the top-level dict and never found it.\n\nThe fix is a one-line change: it now uses `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. This matches what `docs/commands.md` describes.\n\nThe existing test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). I didn't add a regression test for the subcommand case.",
